funded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1680364802", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "145863810", "author": {"steamid": "76561198116784974", "personaname": "SlothMeister", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198116784974/", "num_games_owned": 139, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 5656, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2084, "last_played": 1773872778, "avatar": "90a02ed26d03229bbf64c8b6fa061e46b2a59133"}, "language": "english", "review": "I got Crab Champions on sale for $8, and this is the most fun I have had playing a game in years. I held out on buying it for awhile because the concept seemed so silly, but I was hooked after the first run. The soundtrack is all bangers, too. It's fine on single player (and very challenging on higher difficulties), but definitely more fun with friends. I cannot recommend this game enough.", "timestamp_created": 1694107042, "timestamp_updated": 1694107042, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1680364802", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "145863423", "author": {"steamid": "76561198112198757", "personaname": "Lord Huuh", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/LordHuuh/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 11, "playtime_forever": 887, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 560, "last_played": 1757473015, "avatar": "1c0b5c37a442a2d39f32902ec42f2e26ba6a142e"}, "language": "english", "review": "hella crabs. hella guns. lots of explosions. worth it", "timestamp_created": 1694106596, "timestamp_updated": 1694106596, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1680364802", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "145862107", "author": {"steamid": "76561199279492033", "personaname": "redbeard", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199279492033/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 5, "playtime_forever": 9522, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 4311, "last_played": 1769332911, "avatar": "7ae537b6b7b7b09e68f52e76cdb8f0727f5cb270"}, "language": "english", "review": "very boring", "timestamp_created": 1694105089, "timestamp_updated": 1694105089, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.46012270450592041", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1680364802", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "145860217", "author": {"steamid": "76561198045721162", "personaname": "Houstonruss", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198045721162/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 38, "playtime_forever": 18183, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 18183, "last_played": 1774915777, "avatar": "96eda6be1a0217eeac31417f0b5c48a4361f0b2d"}, "language": "english", "review": "Pretty solid game. Usually well paced, and it's nice getting loot so often.\nMy biggest complaint is at the end of each stage, some specials can spawn, and their Numbers, HP, Damage, and AOE Spam are really unfair. You can have a really nice run going, but lose it because the game will throw you a build check... (your build is decided by RNG)\n\n\nThe march update is a great improvement on most every aspect of the game, I appreciate most all changes and the game definitely plays better. The only glaring problem left for me is the terrible \"AI\" of enemy projectiles. They literally get spammed in random directions and it feels unfair, and if you're playing on true nightmare; you will encounter enemies that spam the entire area consistently.\nRoom-to-room consistency can be rough because you can get a ton of difficult enemies at once, and they all are shooting aoe projectiles at you!\n\nI'm not going to recommend this game until the unfair boss spam is taken care of.\nYou physically cannot dodge all of their stuff, and damage is capped so it's not like you can kill them before they hit you. You WILL be taking damage. You WILL get whittled down slowly, and out of the blue one of the four elites will jump on top of you while you're in full sprint and 1HKO you, because your armor has already been peeled away by 360° spam. (If you even had the luxury of finding armor, and then being able to afford it) ((and armor scales with hp, which you didnt get much of im sure)) (((and this is assuming you even have full hp because the last 5 health chests and shop only had second wind and vitality)))\n\nTrue nightmare sucks to play, but I got to diamond.\nTrue Ultra Chaos is pure bullshte. It's not a challenge; It's fate. You don't win with skill.\n\n-EDIT 2024-\n[strike] Noise has been making good progress in his beta builds, and will have addressed most of my issues.\nNow that the elemental update is live; I feel like I can genuinely reccomend the game to others :) [/strike]\n\n-EDIT 2026-\nCrab champions ain't what it used to be. It's alot more sterile and the trajectory of the game feels bad. Beta after beta new stuff gets added or changed and things get slowly worse and worse.\nIf you want a game where you can choose between baby mode and impossible, here you are. Be bored with prismatic difficulty or rage at \"Full Flex\"\nThe enemies spam bouncing attacks, aoes of damage everywhere, DOT effects, and are all hideously tanky.\nMultiplayer feels awful, it's hard to keep a run going and momentum is halted every time you beat an island or goto the shop.\nLoot distribution and what's shared amongst players is a toss up.\nIt's been years and almost every item pickup looks the same, which is fitting because no item has it's own identity.\n\nNoise, I'm sorry bro but you might have to stick to the music. Good luck with the parkour update, looking forward to islands w/o enemies.", "timestamp_created": 1694103056, "timestamp_updated": 1774916453, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.502157807350158691", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1680364802", "reactions": []}]}